<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Required-reason API declarations.

	  Each reason below is quoted from Apple's published list and matched to a
	  real call site in this app. This file does NOT claim to be exhaustive: it
	  covers the four categories whose APIs were found in this source tree, and
	  a future API addition needs its own entry. An earlier revision of this
	  comment asserted that three of these categories were unused, which was
	  false for all three — do not restate that kind of completeness claim
	  without re-grepping.

	  DiskSpace — E174.1
	    "…check whether there is sufficient disk space to write files… There is
	    an exception that allows the app to avoid downloading files from a
	    server when disk space is insufficient."
	    Call site: DownloadStore.availableCapacityForImportantUsage(), read
	    before a download starts. The observable difference the reason requires
	    is DownloadError.insufficientStorage, which refuses the download and
	    names the shortfall. Never sent off-device.

	  SystemBootTime — 35F9.1
	    "…measure the amount of time that has elapsed between events that
	    occurred within the app or to perform calculations to enable timers."
	    Call sites: ProcessInfo.systemUptime as a monotonic clock in the player
	    and download progress tracking — DownloadProgress, MediaEngineSession,
	    EngineAudioRenderer, PathAHLSFMP4Demuxer. Elapsed intervals only; boot
	    time is never sent.

	  FileTimestamp — C617.1
	    "…access the timestamps, size, or other metadata of files inside the app
	    container, app group container, or the app's CloudKit container."
	    Call site via FileManager.attributesOfItem(atPath:) on files this app
	    wrote: PathAHTTPMediaSource reads .size of a local media file. It reads
	    no timestamp, but it calls the same API the category is about, so it is
	    named here rather than left to be rediscovered.

	  UserDefaults — CA92.1
	    "…read and write information that is only accessible to the app itself."
	    Used throughout for settings this app writes and reads itself. No App
	    Group is involved, so 1C8F.1 does not apply.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>E174.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
